Third-party notice
------------------

The current Android app bundles an Alpine-based runtime, Node, command-line
programs, native libraries, npm dependencies and an unmodified Claude Code binary.
They retain their respective licenses and terms, including copyleft obligations
where applicable. Running a component as a subprocess does not remove its own
redistribution requirements. The retired Termux-based architecture is not the
current runtime.

See `../docs/android-redistribution.md` for executable source collection, retained
notices, and explicitly unresolved coverage and permission requirements. Generated
`assets/legal/` and `backend.tgz:legal/` carry build-specific inventories/notices.
Successful collection or a development build is not complete source coverage or
permission to distribute third-party components.

